YAAP -- Link the Male Human Neutral Tourist

Early in the Gnomish mines, I fell down a trap door.  I read a magic
mapping scroll so that I could quickly go back upstairs, and waited for
my pet to find me.

I went to Minetown and had my pets clear out the guards.  I think I had
2 pets at this time, so I felt that at least one of them would survive
the battle with the watch captain.  The watch  captain dropped a silver
saber, which is great because it doesn't rust.  I went to the bottom of
 the mines hitting most the stuff with the silver saber (so I could
level up on sabers).  The difficult monsters got hit with my broad
pick.  Some monsters got zapped with my camera, so I could run away and
hope my pets would kill them for me.

At the bottom of the mines I collected the gems and luckstone.  Then
spent a while trying to  throw them at the gray unicorn.  After that
adventure was done, my luck was maxed out.  I duel wielded the silver
saber with a runed broadsword, which meant I had 2 rust-proof weapons.
Rust-proof weapons are important since I hit way too many rust traps in
the Gnomish Mines.

I saw a pyrolisk.  I zapped it with my camera and hoped that blind
pyrolisks can't fiery gaze.  They can't.

The big room had some scary monsters, due to them jumping into the
polymorph trap.  There was a minotaur, some high level quadraped, and a
couple other scary things.  So I zapped all the scary monsters with my
camera, and read a scroll of teleportation (which landed me on the
other side  of the level). The scary monsters stumbled around blindly,
while everything else ran across the level toward me.  I killed all the
non-scary monsters as they ran toward me, then killed the scary blind
monsters one by one.

The quest had a second silver saber.

Nothing else exciting happened until I got the castle wand of wishing.
Since the fort didn't get generated this game, I took everything to the
Minetown altar for the "ascension preperation".  I did the mass
identify (shop IDing takes too long, so I shop ID the identify scroll,
and do one big mass identifying after I get the castle wand).  I
polypiled all the  magical junk I collected too.

I genocided all "L" and all "h", and wished of the Orb of Fate.  I
probably could have beaten the game without losing those two conducts,
but I'm still too scared too go polyless/genoless.  There was no way I
could have gone wishless/polyless/genoless, because the game gave me
around 2  scrolls of enchant armor, around 3 scrolls of enchant weapon,
and 0 magic markers.

Nothing exciting happened until the Astral plane.  I found a
non-neutral altar, and then realized that the helm of opposite
alignment probably doesn't work very well on neutral characters.  I
decided not to use the helm, and the second altar ended up being the
neutral altar.


